(area "compaction" :when "the agent works with a result the REPL bound to a name: a large, truncated or printed value it must find, filter, read or show")

(memory "compaction/repl-names" :when "the agent needs a result it computed earlier, does not know what name the REPL bound it to, or is about to retype data the REPL printed"
  "Variable is named after the function that produced it. It always holds the
whole value. setq or defun reports under the name it bound. Never invent a
name: the REPL always tells you the one it bound.

(acme/list-issues :query \"auth bug\")
acme/list-issues-1: list of 27 alists, keys \"id\" \"identifier\" \"title\" \"state\" \"url\"

(+ 1 2)
+-1: 3

(mapcar (lambda (i) (cdr (assoc \"id\" i))) acme/list-issues-1)")

(memory "compaction/echo-window" :when "a printed output came back truncated with a ... line, or the agent needs one part of a long value found"
  "Echo windowing, what it prints:
- (echo x :offset 0 :length n) print a window of x, counted in
  whitespace-separated words. Closing ... line gives offset to continue from.
- (echo x :match \"re\" :context 8 :max 10 :ignore-case t) print only regions
  matching a regex. Each comes as @ and word offset, plus surrounding words,
  match wrapped in double square brackets. Feed reported offset back as
  :offset. Use this to READ a value; use grep to KEEP what matched.
- When you know what you look for: (echo report-1 :match \"pattern\") .
- One unbroken word, minified JSON say, is cut by character, and the ... line
  points at a substring. Several echoes in one step share the budget. When it
  runs out you are told how many words you were not shown.
- Output ending in a ... line is not everything. Do not re-run, do not
  answer from the fragment. Page on with the offset the ... line gives.

Echo output is capped for you; user never sees echo. Past the cap, text stops and
a ... line says how much is left:

... 10 of 40 words shown, 30 below — read on with (echo report-1 :offset 10)")

(memory "compaction/extract" :when "a large result came back and the agent must pick out rows, matches or items: filter, search or count them"
  "Extracting, what each returns:
- Exception to silence: a bare head or tail step prints in full.
- (head x [n]) first n of x; (tail x [n]) last n. On a list, n ELEMENTS:
(head issues 4) is first four rows. On text, n words.
  A slice written as a step of its own is PRINTED and gets no name: you asked
  to read it. Nested in another form it prints nothing, only the value:
(mapcar row (head issues 4)) , (setq top (head issues 4)) .
- (grep x \"pattern\" :group n :max n :ignore-case t) what pattern matched, as a
  list, or nil. On a list, ELEMENTS whose printed form matches:
(grep issues \"auth\") is the issues about auth. On text, matched substrings:
(grep page \"https?://[^ ]+\") is the URLs in it.
- A discovery call prints every name and description, no shape. One call is
  the whole step. Never echo one, never re-run the same search with different
  words, never head it.
- Prefer computing over reading: (length x) , mapcar, assoc and grep work on
  the complete value. One extracting form beats paging through text.

Example. A result named grep-1 holds the URLs of a page:

(grep page-1 \"https?://[^ ]+\")
grep-1: (\"https://x.dev/a\")

(echo (car grep-1))
https://x.dev/a

Bare slice already answers \"what is in there\":

(head acme/list-issues-1 2)
(((\"id\" . \"a1f\") (\"identifier\" . \"ENG-12\") (\"title\" . \"Auth token refresh fails\"))
  ((\"id\" . \"c3d\") (\"identifier\" . \"ENG-31\") (\"title\" . \"OAuth callback drops the state param\")))")

(memory "compaction/doc" :when "the agent is about to call a form whose keywords or arguments it is not sure of, or a call was just rejected"
  "(doc 'name) prints a binding's full signature, whole, free against echo
budget. Look freely. Read it before guessing a keyword. Call rejected: error
names fix? Use it. Names none? Read (doc 'name) .")

(memory "compaction/render-rows" :when "the agent fetched rows of data and must read them, or show them as a table, list or summary"
  "To read rows, keep whole list and echo a rendering of it:

(defun row (i) (concat \"| \" (cdr (assoc \"identifier\" i)) \" | \" (cdr (assoc \"title\" i)) \" |\"))
row: function

(echo (string-join (mapcar row (head acme/list-issues-1 4)) \"\\n\"))
| ENG-12 | Auth token refresh fails |
| ENG-31 | OAuth callback drops the state param |

Both wrong. Never do either:
(echo \"https://x.dev/a\") the URL typed from a printout
(echo \"| ENG-12 | Auth token refresh fails |\") the rows typed out by hand")
